# Operators still looked up by string at run time, as "file operator".
#
# Each line is a global name intern plus a linear walk of the operator
# table, performed every time the code around it runs, and answering a null
# object rather than an error for a name that is not there. The way to
# retire one is XPOST_OP(ctx, <entry>), adding the entry to XPOST_OP_REFS
# in xpost_context.h if it is not already listed there.
#
# tests/check-op-references.sh holds this register to shrinking only: a
# lookup that appears anywhere and is not listed here fails the build, and
# a line here that no longer describes a lookup fails it too.
#
# Nothing is left, and empty is the one size at which "only shrinks" can
# be held to anything: while there was room here, a new lookup passed the
# moment it was written down. So the register is required to stay empty.
# A line added below fails the check, and the way past it is not a line
# but XPOST_OP(ctx, <entry>).
